From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Attard <sattard@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 13:41:43 +0000
Subject: fix: allow Electron's linked bindings under the permission model

https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/65432 made process._linkedBinding()
throw ERR_ACCESS_DENIED when the permission model is enabled without
--allow-addons. Electron exposes all of its built-in modules to JS as
linked bindings (electron_common_*, electron_browser_*, ...), and its
own bootstrap script (node_init and friends) reaches them through
process._linkedBinding(), so with that change `electron --permission`
in ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE mode can no longer initialise Electron's Node.js
integration (ASAR support etc.) and logs a CompileAndCall error.

In an Electron build the linked-binding list only ever contains
Electron's own runtime modules; applications cannot link bindings into
the binary and real native addons still go through process.dlopen(),
which remains gated on --allow-addons. Exempt the electron_* bindings
from the addon check so the runtime can bootstrap, while keeping the
upstream behaviour for any other name.

This can be removed if upstream grows a way for embedders to register
linked bindings that are not treated as addons by the permission model,
or if Electron stops routing its internal bindings through
process._linkedBinding().

diff --git a/src/node_binding.cc b/src/node_binding.cc
index 9f34534d2fa8e52612d4e1d55a39742213046218..ba3f06b8df90bce623e656940a27fae2b4e0206d 100644
--- a/src/node_binding.cc
+++ b/src/node_binding.cc
@@ -670,8 +670,15 @@ void GetLinkedBinding(const FunctionCallbackInfo<Value>& args) {
 
   node::Utf8Value module_name_v(env->isolate(), module_name);
   const char* name = *module_name_v;
-  THROW_IF_INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSIONS(
-      env, permission::PermissionScope::kAddon, module_name_v.ToStringView());
+  // Electron's built-in modules are registered as linked bindings and are
+  // part of the runtime rather than user-supplied addons; Electron's own
+  // bootstrap scripts cannot run without them, so they are not subject to
+  // the addon permission.
+  if (!module_name_v.ToStringView().starts_with("electron_")) {
+    THROW_IF_INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSIONS(env,
+                                      permission::PermissionScope::kAddon,
+                                      module_name_v.ToStringView());
+  }
 
   node_module* mod = nullptr;
 
